# Rule of 110 (Asset Allocation)

A simple heuristic for determining stock and bond allocation: subtract your age from 110 to get the percentage of your portfolio to hold in stocks.

## Examples
- Age 25: 85% stocks, 15% bonds
- Age 35: 75% stocks, 25% bonds
- Age 45: 65% stocks, 35% bonds
- Age 55: 55% stocks, 45% bonds

## Alternative
Use a target-date fund (e.g., VTTHX for 2055 retirement) which automatically adjusts allocation as you age, requiring zero maintenance.

